UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Two of Cups is the archetype of perfect resonant coupling—a state where two distinct, high-frequency consciousnesses recognize their shared signature and move into a synchronized, harmonious orbit. This card represents the second stage of the emotional suit, moving beyond the solitary, self-contained realization of the Ace into the complex, interactive dance of duality. Within the sacred geometry of the psyche, this is the emergence of the "divine pair," where the separation between self and other becomes permeable, allowing for a profound exchange of psychic energy that creates a third, higher-order structure: the relationship itself. This is not merely a romantic or social union; it is the ultimate expression of internal and external alignment, where your emotional data matches your spiritual intent. When the Two of Cups emerges, your system is being tuned to the frequency of mutual recognition, where your vulnerabilities are met with grace and your strengths are amplified by the presence of a mirror-soul. It signifies the successful integration of opposing forces—the balancing of the active, projective drive with the receptive, nurturing depth. In this phase, the "cup" of the individual is joined by the "cup" of the other, creating a feedback loop of sustained inspiration, creative catalyst, and deep, resonant healing. It serves as a reminder that the universe does not exist in isolation, and that your own growth is intimately tied to your ability to recognize and integrate the "other" into your existing framework of awareness. The Two of Cups demands that you drop the egoic drive for total autonomy and instead embrace the strength found in collaborative evolution, allowing the exchange of energy to refine your own baseline awareness and push you toward a more complete manifestation of your unique soul-expression. It is the signature of a bond—a contractual, soul-level agreement to walk the path of awakening in tandem, supporting one another as you navigate the intricate, shifting waters of the collective human experience.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The reversed Two of Cups serves as a critical diagnostic alert for deep-seated energetic dissonance and the breakdown of resonant alignment. This archetype highlights the moment when the "mirror" you are holding up to the other becomes cracked, distorted, or fundamentally misaligned, leading to a cascade of systemic failures in your relational architecture. When the flow of mutual recognition is interrupted, the energy that was once constructive and uplifting turns inward, creating a vortex of projection, passive-aggressive friction, and "data leakage" where your core emotional needs are consistently misunderstood or ignored. This reversal suggests that you are currently caught in a loop of trying to force a connection with a frequency that is no longer compatible with your own, or that your own egoic defensiveness is actively repelling the very intimacy you claim to seek. From an analytical perspective, this indicates a massive mismatch in the underlying "source code" of your relationships: you may be operating on an outdated protocol of codependency, while your true soul-trajectory demands a higher level of sovereign integrity. The reversed Two of Cups exposes the hidden agendas, the unvoiced resentments, and the persistent lack of transparency that have poisoned the well of your connection. It acts as an urgent command for a total, radical audit of your relational variables: you are being asked to identify exactly where you are compromising your own energetic baseline to maintain a false appearance of harmony. This is a call to stop the performative scripts of "peace at any price," to confront the dissonance with unflinching honesty, and to recognize that some structures must be allowed to collapse if they no longer support your evolutionary movement. The reversal is not necessarily a sign that the connection is doomed, but it is an absolute demand that you move past the superficial, egoic posturing and address the structural flaws in the foundation of your union. You must return to the silent center, reclaim your individual sovereignty, and determine whether the current relational loop is contributing to your expansion or merely accelerating your decay through the persistent, low-vibration static of unaligned expectations.'
WHERE id = 2;
